4 0 obj
<<
/Creator ( )
/Producer ( )
/Author (Mounts,Jon S.;Belk,Dave M.;Hughson,Montgomery C.)
/Keywords (*FLUID DYNAMICS;*FINITE DIFFERENCE THEORY;*NUMERICAL ANALYSIS;*USER MANUALS;STABILITY;VISCOUS FLOW;AERODYNAMIC CHARACTERISTICS;FLOW FIELDS;EXTERNAL STORES;CONFIGURATIONS;MODELS;THREE DIMENSIONAL;ERRORS;CONSISTENCY)
/Subject (This report serves as an instructional aid in the analysis of the numerical techniques used in current computational fluid dynamic CFD Flow Solvers. A second-order, explicit predictor-corrector method, developed by MacCormack, is analyzed for stability, convergence , conservative property error, transportive property error, dispersion and phase error, and dissipation error, with respect to the viscous Burgers equation. The viscous Burgers equation is used as a nonlinear analog to the three-dimensional equations typically used in CFD analyses.)
/Title (An Analysis of the Viscous Burgers Equation as Modeled by the MacCormack Method.)
/Filename (/pdf/TR/ADA182763.pdf)
>>
endobj
